From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odonnellmatt <odonnellmatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:53:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/tests: walk the layout editor step by step on the
 Simulator

The harness had stopped linking on this base: hle_lifecycle.c calls
dm_switch2_teardown on the way back to a shell, and the harness does not
build pad_switch2_apple.m. DuoRuntimeStubs.m gets a no-op for it, beside
the harness's other shell stubs.

DuoEditorShotTests runs the editor in the harness app's own window, so
with the device's real size and safe area (a sensor housing, a home
indicator), sideways and then upright: it opens the editor in 3D, chooses
each of the six groups, toggles Each side on its own and Both sides
together on A B X Y, drags the left shoulders down a third of the safe
area, presses the stick's + three times, shows a phone's rest (All
controls, Save for, Reset to default), and opens the editor again in
German and in French (the longest words of the ten languages the NX2Apple
shell passes) for the choice and the rest. After each step it checks the
panel: a phone's bar inside the safe area and off the group just chosen,
Cancel and Done shown and inside it, every control on it at least 44
points, the choice's titles whole; an iPad's card inside the view with
Cancel and Done in it. It then draws the window into
<device>-<orientation>-<NN>-<step>.png in DM_SHOTS (xcodebuild's
TEST_RUNNER_DM_SHOTS) or the app's tmp/editor-shots, with the measures in
<device>-metrics.txt; with DM_SHOTS_SCREEN=1 it waits for a script to take
the Simulator's own screenshot of the step (<name>.req, <name>.done).
Nothing is saved: every editor closes with Cancel. A second test tries the
phone's bar on any device (DM_PAD_EDIT_COMPACT=1) on an iPhone-sized
gamepad outside the window: the bar starts on an edge, goes to the top for
the stick and to the bottom for the shoulders, back to the top when the
shoulders are dragged under it, keeps Cancel, Done and Reset to default
with the rest shown, and folds the rest when a group is chosen.

To turn an iPhone upright for that test the harness app answers the
orientations it takes from duo_harness_orientations (its app and scene
delegates): by default its Info.plist's (an iPhone sideways, an iPad any
way, as test_orientation_policy.py keeps them), upright too while the test
asks.

Checked here (Linux, no Apple SDK): DuoEditorShotTests.m through clang
-fsyntax-only against declaration stubs of the UIKit and XCTest names it
uses; test_orientation_policy.py.

Run on a Mac, on the author's own tree (this series' feature code on
another base): xcodebuild build-for-testing of the harness for the
Simulator, then DuoEditorShotTests (every step and its pictures) and the
editor's seven testLayoutEditor cases of DuoHarnessTests passed on
Simulators of an iPhone SE (3rd generation), an iPhone 17, an iPhone 17 Pro
Max and an 11-inch iPad, held sideways and upright, in English, German and
French. Not run: this exact tree on a Mac, a real iPhone. The harness is
not part of CI.

Upstream-Status: pending [builds on 0020 and 0040: the seedds/nxnative pull request follows once they are upstream]
Reason: walks the layout editor step by step on iPhone and iPad Simulators in the Duo harness, with a picture of each step
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1397 (the feature issue, to be opened before the pull request)
