 The harness uses synthetic host state and does not validate an installed game, physical hinge sensors or device motion.
 
+`DuoEditorShotTests` runs the layout editor (Adjust Gamepad Layout) in the harness app's own window, so on the Simulator's real screen size and safe area: sideways and upright (the harness turns an iPhone upright only for this test), it opens the editor, chooses each group, toggles Both sides together | Each side on its own, drags and resizes a group, shows the rest of a phone's bar, and repeats the choice in German and French. After each step it checks the panel (an iPhone's bar inside the safe area, off the group just chosen, Cancel and Done in reach, every control at least 44 points, the choice's titles whole) and writes a PNG of the window to `DM_SHOTS` (pass `TEST_RUNNER_DM_SHOTS=<folder>` to `xcodebuild`), or to the app's `tmp/editor-shots`. With `TEST_RUNNER_DM_SHOTS_SCREEN=1` it also waits at each step for a script to take the Simulator's own screenshot (`<name>.req`, then `<name>.done`). Its other test tries the phone's bar on any device (`DM_PAD_EDIT_COMPACT=1`).
+
